Subject: [PATCH] libtaskmanager: Add VirtualDesktopGeometries role

A window tiled differently on each of its virtual desktops has another
geometry on each of them. Expose the geometries the compositor reports
for those desktops through a new VirtualDesktopGeometries role.

CCBUG: 506056
---
 libtaskmanager/abstracttasksmodel.h  |  3 +++
 libtaskmanager/waylandtasksmodel.cpp | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 26 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libtaskmanager/abstracttasksmodel.h b/libtaskmanager/abstracttasksmodel.h
index cb6c38f998..e9192e92ec 100644
--- a/libtaskmanager/abstracttasksmodel.h
+++ b/libtaskmanager/abstracttasksmodel.h
@@ -96,6 +96,9 @@ public:
         IsExcludedFromCapture, /**< Whether the task's window has been hidden from screencasts. @since 6.6 */
         StorageId, /** The KService storageId for the underlying service. @since 6.8  */
         IsMapped, /**< Whether the window is mapped, @since 6.8 */
+        VirtualDesktopGeometries, /**< Geometries of the task (i.e. the window) on the virtual
+                                       desktops where they differ from Geometry, as a map from
+                                       virtual desktop id to rect. @since 6.9 */
     };
     Q_ENUM(AdditionalRoles)

